05044d931601f03ae60a21587a8215c8d87f7c20ca1937c914" "q-7892/selection/905664aede55fd46b3faf6009a51c02db70fd843cd7b2823a7eb236d7317d20c" "q-7892/selection/314ba76077d0b22f5a9b984918162821ae7808072a3b1f18c7b0eef50a0465d5" "q-7892/selection/c83d2039eb3271d8e3531ed968dc2bf5c93ac11b0708d963fdc86049daa36b11" "q-7892/selection/8bb20196c2daa0efaa62586848bdae617ad27f5d2c98e35263a003dd44b4b2ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7892" :question/id #uuid "c268af70-f8b6-5cb4-9a8d-a2de421197dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-7892" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+8y=0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={e}^{\\pi },\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=4{e}^{\\pi }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4)-4+8 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda -2 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =2\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={e}^{\\pi }$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-P{e}^{\\pi } & ={e}^{\\pi } \\\\ P & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=4{e}^{\\pi },$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2{e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+{e}^{2x}(-2P\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=4{e}^{\\pi }$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2P{e}^{\\pi }-2Q{e}^{\\pi } & =4{e}^{\\pi } \\\\ -2P-2Q & =4 \\\\ 2-2Q & =4 \\\\ Q & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $P=-1$ and $Q=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\  & =-{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-7892/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20e5f532-d99f-5406-b006-f34aa9074819"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7892"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130371/selection/e325902c85e83ffd4a7e62ee837556a3df0952ef09443b5db08d113a82f55261" :answer/id #uuid "837b078a-9ede-5773-928b-285f4e62a805" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130371/selection/b45f9321884b6506232bbb457d7db07a70c88c7606b8815a5b6de6d08ee45887" :answer/id #uuid "bfbcc6be-0301-57ad-b5c3-721baaa53da5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130371/selection/2fb6094fe655596f1bfb6160de549c457df9d5b8bec2352cdfa7d45d13dd92be" :answer/id #uuid "51d20a33-66f7-51cc-be82-4a87c9e391eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130371/selection/4973efd0a54aef906189fab3aa926254a15f41660043064761e492b8919a2d93" :answer/id #uuid "71545513-3c59-5eae-b70e-a143a3666aba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130371/selection/b08023fa1e4aa1adf7772e7a2ee121e337f66501712d750da12358d56133f53d" :answer/id #uuid "bb7b2a3e-73db-5278-a6df-ee43b48f0357" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130371/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "36ca1596-b14f-546d-926e-91dff972b85a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130371/selection/b08023fa1e4aa1adf7772e7a2ee121e337f66501712d750da12358d56133f53d" :answer-field/choices ["q-130371/selection/e325902c85e83ffd4a7e62ee837556a3df0952ef09443b5db08d113a82f55261" "q-130371/selection/b45f9321884b6506232bbb457d7db07a70c88c7606b8815a5b6de6d08ee45887" "q-130371/selection/2fb6094fe655596f1bfb6160de549c457df9d5b8bec2352cdfa7d45d13dd92be" "q-130371/selection/4973efd0a54aef906189fab3aa926254a15f41660043064761e492b8919a2d93" "q-130371/selection/b08023fa1e4aa1adf7772e7a2ee121e337f66501712d750da12358d56133f53d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130371" :question/id #uuid "95540bc4-4505-5474-9fd4-676a2775e174" :question/math-academy-id "q-130371" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+26y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+26y=0,\\,y(0)=-4,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=-4.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=1,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)+{e}^{x}(-5P\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+5Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=1$ into the above to get\n\n$$\nP+5Q=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=-4$ gives $Q=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130371/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20e5f532-d99f-5406-b006-f34aa9074819"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130371"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130370